  "reason": "A restored snapshot is not a durable effect ledger. It carries globals, functions, classes, time budget and, for a mid-feed snapshot, the paused call stack — but it does not authenticate, authorize, or record confirmed/unresolved effects. The reference is explicit: 'A dump must come from a trusted compatible producer with verified integrity. Interpreter bytes are not approval, authentication or a durable effect ledger.' (sempai-monty-compatibility.md L92-106, card be447cba9594). It also states 'Neither restored memory nor a timeout establishes that no effect happened' and forbids 'replay[ing] a whole Recipe or a completed operation after an output/reply failure' (be447cba9594). tools.md reinforces this: 'A VM crash, timeout or reply-database failure must not automatically replay the entire Recipe or reset its Tool attempt counts. Preserve confirmed effects. Expose unknown effect status as unresolved and use supported operation-specific status lookup, durable deduplication or explicit reconciliation before deciding whether the approved retry contract permits another dispatch. Without such evidence, do not replay the operation or claim exactly-once external execution.' (tools.md L313-371, card b1c9eb6c27e7). A timeout or missing completion record does not prove no effect occurred, and unknown completion may be retried only under an explicitly approved safe contract with read-only or durable deduplication evidence — not merely by restoring memory. (skills.md L497-551, card 5dba8e21f131; tools.md L235-264, card 00ad86a8783c). Therefore, restoring a snapshot by itself does not authorize replaying an unresolved external operation; reconciliation through supported persistence, status lookup, or deduplication is required first."
